# These CVEs require docker/cli or docker/docker to be upgraded to v29+.
# The v29 release series changed the Go module path and broke API compatibility
# with the interfaces used in this alauda/v0.10.4 branch.  A full port is
# out-of-scope for a security-only sweep; both entries are documented here so
# that trivy CI does not fail on findings that cannot be resolved without a
# major refactor.
#
# CVE-2025-15558 — docker/cli: Windows-only privilege escalation via malicious
#   plugin binaries.  Fixed in docker/cli v29.2.0.  This branch uses
#   v23.0.3+incompatible; upgrading to v29 is incompatible with the v0.10.4 API.
#   Impact is Windows-only; BuildKit in production runs on Linux.
CVE-2025-15558

# CVE-2026-34040 — Moby/docker: Authorization bypass vulnerability.
#   Fixed in docker/docker v29.3.1.  This branch uses v26.1.5+incompatible;
#   upgrading to v29 requires a major module-path change and API refactor.
CVE-2026-34040

# CVE-2026-33997 — Moby/docker: Privilege escalation vulnerability.
#   Fixed in docker/docker v29.3.1.  Same root cause as CVE-2026-34040 above;
#   both require the v29 module-path migration which is out-of-scope here.
CVE-2026-33997
